harness: jxl-encoder/examples/lz77_hash_ab.rs + scripts/lz77_hash_ab_join.py
arms:    JXL_LZ77_MURMUR_HASH unset (fold, shipped) vs =1 (post-v0.12 Murmur, #110 item 1)
chain:   JXL_LZ77_MAX_CHAIN in {1,8,256}; 256 is the shipped default (#110 item 3)
content: photo   = imazen-26 png-v3 .hdr.png 16-bit centre crops
         lineart = imazen26-float-synth (procedural line art/polygons/grids/gradients,
                   generated by scripts/gen_float_lineart_corpus.py to fill the
                   photographic-only gap in the #109 F5 measurement)
depths:  u8 / u16 / f32 built from identical 16-bit source content
efforts: lossless e8 (Greedy) + e9 (Optimal); lossy e9 (Optimal). Rle efforts
         never construct a HashChain, so they cannot be affected.
timing:  chain-length wall figures are process-level INTERLEAVED, 3 reps, min per
         arm. The earlier block-ordered runs are NOT usable for wall (they
         reported chain=1 as slower, an artifact of run order).
host:    Mac aarch64
